  smallest q where the reduced residues are NOT an additive coset: 3

what that predicts, against the paper's two theorems
  q=4 : reduced = odd residues = additive coset  -> the floor applies
        M_odd(4) = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.707107   and this is the extremal modulus for a
        random odd sequence (thm:modfour, proved).
  q=6 : reduced = {1,5}, NOT an additive coset  -> the floor does not apply
        M(6) = sqrt(3)/2 = 0.866025  survives, and this is the extremal modulus for
        the primes (Part II, proved).  M_odd(6) = 0 because the odd residue 3 is
        present for an odd sequence and cos(pi/2) = 0 -- the vanishing lemma.

